# ---------------------------------------------------------------------------
# BUG 9 fix: MAP4 absolute-addressing entry points (0x05/0x0D/0x15/0x1D).
# These are literal top-level first bytes (A2[] dispatches them straight into
# MAP4), NOT opcode47-gated EA bytes -- no EA prefix at all. Real layout:
#   [literal instr8 byte][addr8/addr16 payload][MAP4 dispatch byte]
# The dispatch byte reuses the same opcode_special mnemonic values as the
# existing MAP3/MAP4 single-operand instructions (tst=0x16, clr=0x13, etc.),
# just addressing a literal absolute address instead of an EA token.
#
# Confirmed against live RVR 1998 ROM bytes for the 0x15/0x1D (16-bit
# absolute) forms, dispatch values 0x16 (tst) and 0x13 (clr):
#   0x20b10: 1D EF 98 16  -> tst.w @0xEF98:16
#   0x20d98: 1D EF A2 16  -> tst.w @0xEFA2:16
#   0x1736d: 15 02 E3 16  -> tst.b @0x02E3:16
#   0x246c1: 1D F2 52 13  -> clr.w @0xF252:16
#
# 0x05/0x0D (8-bit absolute forms) are not yet confirmed against a live
# instance -- do not add until verified the same way, per README guidance.
# Other head-table mnemonics (neg/not/tas/shal/shar/shll/shlr/rotl/rotr/
# rotxl/rotxr) are pending the same per-mnemonic byte verification.
# ---------------------------------------------------------------------------


