# pre-existing ISA-level ambiguity between bra's 16-bit-offset encoding and
# rtd's 8-bit-displacement encoding sharing the same opcode byte - not
# something this fix can resolve without deeper investigation into how real
# hardware/IDA disambiguates the two (likely on a later byte, not this one).
# Left as a known limitation: the 16-bit bra encoding still keeps a spurious
# fallthrough edge. Flagging in HANDOFF.md rather than guessing at a fix here.

